# The earliest time this image boots with, UTC.
#
# A unit has no real-time clock, so a cold boot starts at the image's epoch —
# earlier than the notBefore of a public certificate the payload's peer
# presents — and a TLS handshake to that peer fails until NTP has synchronised
# the clock. brenn-clock-floor raises the clock to this value before the time
# client starts. NTP over the wired link, from a time server the DHCP lease
# names, is the real fix; this is the stopgap for a TLS consumer running on an
# unsynchronised clock. TODO(app-payload-cold-clock): the unit, its script and
# this file go when that entry closes.
#
# It goes stale when the peer's certificate renews past it (a Let's Encrypt
# leaf renews about every sixty days), and is bumped then, by an image build.
#
# Deliberately not SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH (image/config/brenn-common.yaml): that
# value also selects the Debian snapshot, and the ext4 build lowers every later
# file timestamp to it, which is why the floor is this file's content and not
# any file's mtime.
#
# Exactly one non-comment line, in the form 2026-09-27T00:00:00Z.
2026-09-27T00:00:00Z
